+## Removing people
+
+Administrators can permanently erase people from the user list, including accounts
+previously deactivated by Remove. Erasure deletes their account, sign-in history,
+reading marks, access grants, and books that are not shared with everyone (including
+content, revisions, and search entries). Books shared with everyone keep their
+content and readers, but lose their creator link and use the byline "Deleted author".
+
+File cleanup uses Active Storage's post-commit purge jobs, including uploads and
+image variants. Keep the background workers running to complete file erasure;
+files still used by retained content are not purged. Independently retained
+backups must be handled under your backup retention/erasure procedures.
+
